# tilted_bore.cam — a pocket built against the intruder with an axis (Phase 41
# slice 5; DECISIONS.md → "Phase 41 slice 5…").
#
# `Drain` is a bore whose axis is NOT vertical: it enters the top face at
# (70, 40) and leans toward -X at 30° from vertical, 14mm deep. No op here
# cuts it — a 3-axis program never tilts the tool, so it is cut on another
# setup — and every verb that names it refuses by name. It is declared so
# the pocket's boundary can be BUILT AGAINST it: looking down the tool axis
# the bore is not its mouth (a circle) nor its section at the pocket's floor
# (an ellipse) but its plan ENVELOPE over the whole slab it spans — two
# lines a diameter apart along the lean, joined by the far halves of its two
# end sections — because the cylinder leans, and above the floor it overhangs
# what the floor section reaches.
#
# The pocket's right wall is an arc through (58, 20) and (58, 60) tangent to
# that envelope pushed out 3mm — the web the machinist wants left between the
# pocket and the hole — chorded by the construction itself:
#
#     nacs --arc '58,20 58,60 tangent=Drain offset=3 pick=2' tilted_bore.cam
#
# pasted as the loop lines below (the first answer, the larger arc around the
# far side of the hole, is the one that wraps the bore; the second bulges
# into the pocket and kisses the near cap at (51.994, 40)). The grammar gained
# no arc: the file holds points, as every curved footprint does, and the
# parser is the only judge. `nacs --outline` lists Drain under "unused" —
# honestly: the construction is an authoring step, not a thing the engine
# reads at generation.
units mm
feed 800
plunge 300
rapid_z 5
clearance_z 25
spindle 3000

stock Box(w=100, l=80, h=20, x=0, y=0, z=0)

tool T5 Endmill(dia=10.0)

feature Drain TiltedBore(dia=12, extent=14, x=70, y=40, tilt=30, heading=180)

feature Pocket ProfilePocket(extent=8
    10 20
    58.000 20.000
    57.100 21.435
    56.267 22.911
    55.505 24.424
    54.814 25.971
    54.196 27.549
    53.652 29.154
    53.184 30.782
    52.792 32.431
    52.477 34.095
    52.241 35.773
    52.083 37.460
    52.004 39.153
    52.004 40.847
    52.083 42.540
    52.241 44.227
    52.477 45.905
    52.792 47.569
    53.184 49.218
    53.652 50.846
    54.196 52.451
    54.814 54.029
    55.505 55.576
    56.267 57.089
    57.100 58.565
    58.000 60.000
    10 60
)

run Clear(tool=T5, profile=Pocket, stepover=4.0)
